  "interpretation": "At sim time 11.583 s, the adapter locked because its latest accepted telemetry source stamp (11.254 s) was 329 ms old, exceeding the configured 300 ms source-age limit; its measured sim receipt age was 281 ms, below the 500 ms limit. The adapter-local telemetry callback had entered 9 ms before the lock, but its latest accepted source stamp was still 11.254 s. Other accepted inputs at that instant remained within their guards. A separate raw VINS subscriber saw initialized telemetry continue through 48.841 s; its maximum source-stamp gap was 165 ms, including a 165 ms interval around the lock. This supports a delivery/scheduling delay or backlog at the adapter telemetry intake rather than a demonstrated VINS source outage. The data does not separate DDS reader behavior, executor scheduling, or header age at the publisher-to-adapter boundary. The run-local diagnostic added counters and did not alter the health decision.",
